  const writingStyles = { natural:'自然细腻', cinematic:'电影感', literary:'文学抒情', concise:'克制简洁', suspense:'悬疑紧张', daily:'生活流' };
  const writingStylePrompts = {
    natural:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: Wang Zengqi\'s use of food, objects, weather, and local routines to make a setting credible, with feeling carried by what people do; and Chekhov\'s use of hesitation, self-correction, ineffective gestures, and material circumstances to reveal contradiction without diagnosing the character. [BLENDING METHOD] Select two or three concrete details already present in the scene, then let action and dialogue change the relationship. Narrate only what the viewpoint character can presently perceive. Do not name an emotion when behavior can carry it. Vary sentence length with the speed of action. End on a specific change that remains open to response. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] She returned the second set of chopsticks to the cupboard, shut the door, opened it again, and asked whether he still wanted scallions in the soup.',
    cinematic:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: the distance between surface dialogue and actual intent in Hemingway\'s Hills Like White Elephants, where pauses and evasions carry crucial information; and the clear blocking, physical action, and object states used to propel scenes in Dashiell Hammett\'s The Maltese Falcon. [BLENDING METHOD] Establish the positions of people, exits, and consequential objects, then alternate action, dialogue, and environmental consequence. Use shorter sentences under pressure and longer observation during quiet intervals. Never use camera terminology. Do not explain what the visible action has already established. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] The lock clicked twice. Fang Yikai did not turn around. He slid the second cup behind the newspaper.',
    literary:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: Shen Congwen\'s integration of landscape, daily order, and human fate in Border Town; Calvino\'s structural repetition and light conceptual architecture in Invisible Cities; and Virginia Woolf\'s close sensory attention, where a present object briefly opens memory before returning to the room. [BLENDING METHOD] Images must come from objects that truly exist in the current scene and must later affect meaning or action. Perception and memory may briefly overlap, but narration must promptly return to physical space and ongoing action. Keep figurative language sparse. Never announce a theme or moral. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] At the sixth bell, Su Qian folded the letter along its old crease. The umbrellas below had dispersed; the cut left by the paper still marked her finger.',
    concise:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: Hemingway\'s omission of explanation so facts, actions, and dialogue carry subtext; and Raymond Carver\'s use of kitchens, bills, ashtrays, and unfinished speech to create relational pressure. [BLENDING METHOD] Prefer exact verbs and concrete nouns. Remove modifiers that do not change meaning. Each paragraph completes one action or exchange without restating known information. Dialogue may be brief, but it needs a clear addressee and immediate purpose. Silence must be shown through an interrupted action, an unanswered question, or unfinished work. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] He finished reading the bill and placed his phone facedown. “Next month.” The refrigerator stopped humming. The tap continued to drip.',
    suspense:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: Agatha Christie\'s control over the order of clues, allowing ordinary details to acquire new meaning later; Borges\'s use of catalogues, maps, mirrored structures, and branching time; and Edgar Allan Poe\'s accumulation of pressure through enclosed spaces, recurring sounds, and altered objects. [BLENDING METHOD] Add only one verifiable fact per paragraph. Clues must arise from behavior, spatial change, object state, or conflicting testimony. Misdirection must remain retrospectively explainable; never invent the answer at the reveal. Fear should grow from narrowing choices, not exaggerated emotional vocabulary. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] The roster showed that no one entered the archive overnight. Fang Yikai turned it over. His signature appeared beside 3:00 a.m., and the ink had not dried.',
    daily:'[CRAFT REFERENCES] Draw only on broad, non-copying techniques: Wang Zengqi\'s attention to food, seasons, and practiced hands; Lao She\'s dialogue shaped by profession, social position, and relational distance; and Jane Austen\'s judgments, misunderstandings, and social calibration beneath polite speech. [BLENDING METHOD] Build scenes around meals, travel, errands, tidying, and pauses in work. Let relationships shift through forms of address, division of labor, avoidance, jokes, and minor friction. Dialogue may pause, self-correct, or answer sideways. Do not manufacture quotable aphorisms. [ORIGINAL DEMONSTRATION — NEVER COPY OR PARAPHRASE] Su Qian said she did not eat breakfast. Ten minutes later, she took half a slice of toast from Fang Yikai\'s plate. He moved the jam toward her without comment.'
  };
  const styleExecutionFramework = `
 [SCOPE] Apply this style to relationships, psychological change, physical action, and continuous narrative. Style governs narrative organization and verbal texture only. It must never overwrite a character's education, personality, knowledge, identity, or habitual voice.
[RESPONSIBILITY BOUNDARIES] Plot determines what happens. Character data determines what a character knows and would do. Style determines which details receive attention, when information appears, and how sentences carry relational change. Never grant a character knowledge outside the established setting. Never use narration to make the character deliver the author's opinion.
[PARAGRAPH ENGINE] Every paragraph must create a verifiable change: position, object state, new information, relational distance, an executed decision, or a revised judgment. Begin from the current scene, develop action or cognition, and end on a fact that permits the next response. Atmosphere without progression is insufficient.
[DETAIL ADMISSION RULE] Keep a detail only when it affects a choice, changes the meaning of a line, exposes a relational habit, plants a later clue, or revises the reader's judgment. Remove decorative clothing, weather, streetscape, and furnishing details with no function. Prefer precise nouns to chains of adjectives, while respecting the character's era, profession, and knowledge.
[PSYCHOLOGICAL SEQUENCE] First show the observable trigger. Then show judgment, self-defense, or hesitation. Finally let action carry the consequence. A character may misunderstand themself; narration must not turn conflict into a diagnosis or life lesson.
[DIALOGUE FUNCTION] Every spoken line must perform at least one task: ask, evade, test, refuse, confirm, redirect, or alter the relationship. Length follows character habit and scene pressure. Silence must cause a consequence and appear through interrupted action, a displaced answer, or unfinished work.
[EXAMPLE BOUNDARY] Preset examples demonstrate only information density and action order. Never copy or closely paraphrase their names, object combinations, sentence endings, or relational situations. Derive all new material from the current characters, location, era, and history.
[FINAL SELF-CHECK] Check every paragraph for concrete progression, clear pronoun reference, out-of-character knowledge, actions or thoughts imposed on the user, duplicated emotional explanation, decorative sentences removable without loss, and whether the ending preserves space for the user to act. Rewrite failures before producing the answer.`;
  const antiClichePrompt = `[ANTI-CLICHE AND ANTI-TEMPLATE RULES]
1. Do not use empty elevation, concluding morals, summaries of the user's input, serial parallelism, adjective piles, or lyrical sentences that add no information. Avoid stock phrases equivalent to “the gears of fate,” “the air seemed frozen,” or “this moment became eternal.”
2. Avoid prefabricated similes and metaphors. In Chinese output, do not use structures such as “像……一样,” “像……的……,” “像是……,” or “仿佛.” Do not use false-elevation structures such as “不是……而是……,” “这不是……,” or “那不是…….” Do not use “我看过太多” to manufacture world-weariness.
3. Never use pebbles, ripples, feathers, scalpels, needles, or branding irons as emotional or sensory metaphors. Avoid vague or inflated Chinese expressions such as “泛白,” “极其,” “一丝,” “不易察觉,” “不容置疑,” “共犯,” and “震动.” A literal object with the same name is allowed only when physically present and consequential to the scene; it may not serve as a metaphor.
4. Convert abstractions into observable mechanics: how light reaches an object, what pressure touches skin, how distance changes, how weight shifts, and what happens to breath, hands, gaze, or voice. Do not announce atmosphere or emotion for the reader.
5. Character data is a behavioral constraint, never material for self-exposition. Unless directly asked or logically required in the scene, a character must not explain, list, or advertise their background, identity, traits, abilities, or relationships. Rewrite any line that sounds like a profile, lore document, or character card. Show identity through choices, habits, tone, actions, and reactions.
6. Advance the scene through specific action, sensory fact, natural dialogue, and responses consistent with identity. Never decide the user's actions, thoughts, feelings, or dialogue. Output no analysis, writing notes, or restatement of these rules.
7. The final Chinese prose must use natural paragraphing. Each paragraph should carry one principal action, one development in dialogue, or one psychological turn. Insert a blank line between paragraphs. Never compress the response into a single wall of text.`;
  const povLabels = { first:'第一人称“我”', second:'第二人称“你”', third:'第三人称（真名或“他/她”）' };
  function narrationRule(roleName, userName, rolePov, userPov) { const povRules = { first:'first person (“我”)', second:'second person (“你”)', third:'third person (the real name or the appropriate “他/她”)' }; return `Use ${povRules[rolePov] || povRules.first} for the character “${roleName}”. Use ${povRules[userPov] || povRules.second} for the user “${userName}”. In third person, use the real name or the pronoun supported by the character data. If gender is not explicit, prefer the real name and never guess. Pronoun reference must remain unambiguous; do not confuse “我,” “你,” and names within the same paragraph. ${antiClichePrompt}`; }
  function readWritingStyles() { try { const list = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(writingStyleKey) || '[]'); return Array.isArray(list) ? list.filter(item => item?.id && item?.name && item?.prompt) : []; } catch { return []; } }
  function styleOptions() { return `${Object.entries(writingStyles).map(([value, label]) => `<option value="${value}">${label}</option>`).join('')}${readWritingStyles().map(item => `<option value="${esc(item.id)}">${esc(item.name)} · 自定义</option>`).join('')}`; }
  function resolveWritingStyle(id) { const custom = readWritingStyles().find(item => item.id === id); const builtInId = writingStyles[id] ? id : 'natural'; const preset = custom ? { id:custom.id, name:custom.name, prompt:custom.prompt } : { id:builtInId, name:writingStyles[builtInId], prompt:`${writingStylePrompts[builtInId]}${styleExecutionFramework}` }; const edited = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-detail]')?.value.trim(); return { ...preset, prompt:edited || preset.prompt }; }
  function mountWritingStyleDetail() { const styleField = app.querySelector('.ifspace-style-field'); const editor = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-editor]'); if (!styleField || !editor || app.querySelector('[data-if-style-detail]')) return; const wordCount = app.querySelector('[data-if-word-count]'); if (wordCount) wordCount.value = '1500'; const field = document.createElement('div'); field.className = 'ifspace-style-detail'; field.innerHTML = '<span>具体文风要求</span><textarea data-if-style-detail maxlength="5000" placeholder="具体描述语言、节奏、对白、描写重点与需要避免的表达……"></textarea><small>内置文风包含作者技法、融合方法、原创示例和完整执行规则；可以继续修改后另存。</small><button type="button" data-if-style-detail-save>保存文风</button>'; styleField.append(field, editor); const select = app.querySelector('[data-if-writing-style]'); const sync = () => { const textarea = field.querySelector('textarea'); if (textarea) textarea.value = ''; const style = resolveWritingStyle(select?.value || 'natural'); if (textarea) textarea.value = style.prompt; }; select?.addEventListener('change', sync); sync(); }
  function saveCurrentWritingStyle() { const select = app.querySelector('[data-if-writing-style]'); const prompt = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-detail]')?.value.trim(); if (!prompt) return window.alert('请先填写具体文风要求。'); const list = readWritingStyles(); const custom = list.find(item => item.id === select?.value); if (custom) { custom.prompt = prompt; localStorage.setItem(writingStyleKey, JSON.stringify(list)); window.alert(`文风“${custom.name}”已保存。`); return; } const editor = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-editor]'); const detail = app.querySelector('.ifspace-style-detail'); const promptInput = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-prompt]'); const nameInput = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-name]'); if (promptInput) promptInput.value = prompt; if (nameInput) nameInput.value = `${writingStyles[select?.value] || '自定义文风'}副本`; if (detail) detail.hidden = true; if (editor) editor.hidden = false; nameInput?.focus(); }
  function icon(type) { const paths = { plus:'<path d="M24 9v30M9 24h30"/>', back:'<path d="M30 10 16 24l14 14"/>', spark:'<path d="m24 7 4 13 13 4-13 4-4 13-4-13-13-4 13-4z"/>', send:'<path d="m8 23 31-13-9 29-7-13zM8 23l15 3"/>', close:'<path d="m14 14 20 20M34 14 14 34"/>' }; return `<svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true">${paths[type] || ''}</svg>`; }
  function rolePicker() { const list = roles(); return `<div class="ifspace-sheet"><div class="ifspace-sheet-backdrop" data-if-close-sheet></div><section><header><h2>选择参与角色</h2><button type="button" data-if-close-sheet aria-label="关闭">${icon('close')}</button></header><div class="ifspace-role-list">${list.length ? list.map(item => `<button type="button" data-if-role="${esc(item.id)}"><i>${avatar(item)}</i><span><b>${esc(roleRealName(item))}</b><small>${esc(item.identity || '角色')}</small></span><em>${item.id === state.roleId ? '✓' : '›'}</em></button>`).join('') : '<p class="ifspace-empty">请先在聊天 App 中添加角色。</p>'}</div></section></div>`; }
  function newSpace() { return `<section class="ifspace-create"><header><button type="button" data-if-home aria-label="返回">${icon('back')}</button><div><small>新的可能</small><h1>创建一个 if 时空</h1></div></header><main><div class="ifspace-create-intro"><span>时空种子 / 001</span><p>写下一个假设，或者让宇宙替你决定。</p><button type="button" data-if-random><i>✦</i><b>随机灵感</b><small>随机生成</small></button></div><label>这个世界如果……<textarea data-if-premise placeholder="例如：如果我们没有错过"></textarea></label><label>时空风格<input data-if-setting placeholder="例如：温柔日常、末日生存、古代江湖"></label><label>想从哪里开始<input data-if-opening placeholder="例如：第一次在图书馆见面"></label><div class="ifspace-create-options"><label class="ifspace-style-field">文风<div><select data-if-writing-style>${styleOptions()}</select><button type="button" data-if-style-new>＋ 新建</button></div></label><label>每次回复字数<input data-if-word-count type="number" min="50" max="5000" step="50" value="1500" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="输入字数"></label><label>角色「${esc(roleRealName(role()))}」的人称<select data-if-role-pov><option value="first" selected>第一人称 · 我</option><option value="second">第二人称 · 你</option><option value="third">第三人称 · 真名 / 他 / 她</option></select></label><label>用户「${esc(userRealName(role()?.id))}」的人称<select data-if-user-pov><option value="first">第一人称 · 我</option><option value="second" selected>第二人称 · 你</option><option value="third">第三人称 · 真名 / 他 / 她</option></select></label></div><section class="ifspace-style-editor" data-if-style-editor hidden><div><span>新建文风</span><button type="button" data-if-style-close aria-label="关闭">×</button></div><label>文风名称<input data-if-style-name maxlength="24" placeholder="例如：冷冽电影感"></label><label>具体写作要求<textarea data-if-style-prompt maxlength="5000" placeholder="描述用词、节奏、氛围、对话和叙事偏好……"></textarea></label><button type="button" data-if-style-save>保存并使用此文风</button></section><button class="ifspace-primary" type="button" data-if-create>${icon('spark')} 生成这个时空</button></main></section>`; }
  function saveWritingStyle() { const name = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-name]')?.value.trim(); const prompt = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-prompt]')?.value.trim(); if (!name || !prompt) return window.alert('请填写文风名称和具体写作要求。'); const list = readWritingStyles(); const item = { id:`custom-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6)}`, name, prompt }; list.push(item); localStorage.setItem(writingStyleKey, JSON.stringify(list)); const select = app.querySelector('[data-if-writing-style]'); if (select) { select.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `<option value="${esc(item.id)}">${esc(item.name)} · 自定义</option>`); select.value = item.id; } const detailInput = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-detail]'); if (detailInput) detailInput.value = prompt; const detail = app.querySelector('.ifspace-style-detail'); if (detail) detail.hidden = false; const editor = app.querySelector('[data-if-style-editor]'); if (editor) editor.hidden = true; }
  function randomizeWorld() { const pool = pairRandomWorlds.length ? pairRandomWorlds : randomWorlds; let index = Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length); if (pool.length > 1 && index === lastRandomWorld) index = (index + 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * (pool.length - 1))) % pool.length; lastRandomWorld = index; const idea = pool[index]; const premise = app.querySelector('[data-if-premise]'); const setting = app.querySelector('[data-if-setting]'); const opening = app.querySelector('[data-if-opening]'); if (premise) premise.value = idea.premise; if (setting) setting.value = idea.setting; if (opening) opening.value = idea.opening; app.querySelector('.ifspace-create-intro')?.classList.remove('is-randomized'); requestAnimationFrame(() => app.querySelector('.ifspace-create-intro')?.classList.add('is-randomized')); }
